# Commit after every change

When you finish a user-requested change in this repository (code, config, or docs):

1. Ensure the working tree reflects only that work.
2. Create a git commit with a concise message focused on **why**.
3. Do not push unless the user asks.

If a change fails or is incomplete, do not commit until it is fixed or the user stops the task.

This project expects frequent small commits rather than batching unrelated edits.
